glen herrmannsfeldt <gah@ugcs.caltech.edu> wrote:

> For my original comment, I was thinking that the ftp program
> was separate from the underlying TCP/IP system, but maybe that
> isn't true.  I believe I used multinet about 20 years ago, but
> not since then.  

FTP predates TCP/IP by quite a number of years. It is first described in
RFC 114 from 1971. In 1973, after many an RFC, the TCP protocol was
essentially as we know it now - but running on top of NCP and not
TCP/IP (which dates from 1980).

