Start by checking the blower fan coil with an ohmmeter. If it isn't
burnt out, can you spin the fan easily with a  finger? If not, it may
just need some oil. I don't know what type of fan is used in the 3300,
but you can often get to the end of the shaft by removing the paper
label in the middle. I have repaired many equipmentt fans with a drop
of oil -- they just dry up.

If the fan is OK, is there any voltage across it? If not, the circuit
controlling it may be faulty, and this is a more serious problem in
the power supply, or maybe the motherboard.

> - In the worst case (and probable... sigh) of having a dead blower,
> anyone coud be so kind to point me to the Part Number and any idea of
> where I could get a "new" (new as "functioning") one?
>
> Thanks in advance!

The label (before you scape it off to apply oil :) should tell you the
voltage and wattage of the fan. Any good electronic components
supplier should have something that will fit. I might even have one
here.

Chris


