Well, I think the blowers (there are two of them) are innocent. I didn't 
know they were two... I thought they were tho in the BA213 and only one 
in the BA215, but I was wrong. When I have seen the two fans I've though 
  the probability of BOTH dying at the same time should be negligible, 
and when I power on the machine, none of both starts blowing.

Oh, by the way, they are not stuck. They turn easily and sweetly...

So my current suspicious are the power supply and the fan assembly 
cable. And now comes the funny part. Being as well engineered as all DEC 
hardware I've put my hands on (disclaimer: I'm a software guy), it 
surprises me that the power supply gets the electricity from the mains 
THROUGH the fan assembly (I'd say the AC filter is in the very same fan 
assembly), and to take out the fans I've got to extract the power supply 
first.

The fans get their DC power from a cord attached to the backplane. So, 
to test if they get energy, the power supply has to be in its place.

Now I'm in a chicken-and-egg situation, since I can't test if the power 
supply supplies power to the fans without puting it on place, and the 
power supply does not get any AC current without the fan assembly in its 
place...

And here I am. Stuck. :) Any ideas?


